    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0894" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg770"/>

                <head>No. 457.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 23,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Say to Mexican Government that the President very earnestly requests that any
                    contemplated hostilities against Guatemala may be suspended at least until the
                    views of this government can be fully communicated.</p>
                <p>Instructions are now mailed, and United States tenders its good offices in the
                    interest of peace.</p>
                <p>You will co-operate with Doctor Herrera, Guatemalan minister, in all wise steps
                    looking to peace and friendly adjustment of all troubles.</p>
                <closer><signed>BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
